Z||000000||Ozzy||03-25-2000||01:47 AM||||Hey Gang...<P>So, today I finally took the plunge into V6 Fiero land!<P>Ironic that I moned so much about no good deals in the north west...'87 GT, blue, CC, Man 5 spd, AC, PW, PL, PM, tilt, Custom rims, Grey int.  120k  = $2,600.00! Dealer wanted more but I chewed him down.<P>Car is pretty clean overall. Has one cracked sail panel, crack in the rear exhaust manifold, clutch has the usual hydraulic problems and the power locks need attention. They work but seem froze up. Power mirrors work side to side and down but not up. Emergency brake release needs attention. Also the infamous 'pinned temp guage' problem.<P>Paint is clean with very few marks. Needs rubber and front wheel bearings soon.<P>I drove it today and the 5 spd seems to shift well. Seems high gearded compared to my Coupe. Luv the pickup though!!!!<P>I'm going to have to drive back down to Eugene to pick it tomorrow so I guess the 4 hr drive back will reveal any other problems it has. <P>Happy OZZZY||||reg||6
Z||000001||GT Bastard||03-25-2000||03:06 PM||||Congrats on your purchase!  I'm convinced that 87 is the BEST year for the Fiero.  Then again, that's probably because MINE is an 87.  Have fun and keep us posted!||||reg||1
